From e00ca0bfbb8227e5fa906b1b376eaa9fac44c460 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valisolaris <valisolaris@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:27:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] windows-port: Phase 4 UX round (tree sidebar, split-open,
 Sixel, paste-burst fix)

Bundles the Phase 4 UX-improvement round agreed with the user on top of
the frozen spec (spec/spec.md, spec/decisions.md unchanged):

- Sidebar file tree: multiple directories can stay expanded at once
  (sidebar_files/{mod,files,navigation}.rs), with a scroll-offset fix so
  clicking an already-visible row doesn't snap it to the bottom line
  (ui/sidebar.rs, regression test in sidebar_files::tests).
- Opening a file from the sidebar (Enter/o) now splits a new pane to the
  right instead of overwriting the active pane's tabs
  (Mux::split_with_command/split_with_browser in mux.rs, session/mod.rs,
  app.rs).
- Sixel-encoded in-TUI HTML preview behind an opt-in browser.sixel config
  flag, since Windows Terminal stable supports Sixel but not kitty
  graphics (ui/graphics.rs, ui/graphics_writer.rs, png crate dependency).
- Alt+X to close the active tab/pane, and a Sessions sidebar view listing
  every tab across every pane/screen/workspace (app.rs, config.rs,
  ui/mod.rs, ui/sidebar.rs, localization.rs).
- Paste-burst workaround for Windows crossterm 0.29 not emitting
  Event::Paste: batches same-frame character keys into a synthetic paste
  event so multi-line clipboard paste doesn't submit line-by-line
  (app.rs: read_input_batch/pasteable_char/finish_paste_burst).

Real-machine verified by the user: tab-group drag&drop merge, Sixel
preview, clipboard paste, and the sidebar tree (after the scroll-offset
fix above). Opening a file with Enter into a new split pane is still
unverified on real hardware; see spec/handoff-phase4.md.
